  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-5TO10-R5-004$qb$, $qb$A3-05$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$When negotiating project scope adjustments with a client under tight budget limits, what represents the most effective approach? The decision affects two commitments and requires a visible trade-off rather than a private compromise.$qb$, $qb$Evaluating core underlying priorities to rebalance deliverable scope while protecting project margin boundaries.$qb$, $qb$Offering a standard percentage price reduction immediately to demonstrate goodwill and secure contract agreement.$qb$, $qb$Reiterating standard rate card policies firmly and advising the client that adjustments are unavailable.$qb$, $qb$Escalating the negotiation directly to executive leadership to determine if margin exceptions can be granted.$qb$, $qb$Accepting all requested scope additions at current pricing to maintain positive client sentiment.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
