  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-17TO25-R06-001$qb$, $qb$A3-02$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$A confidential portfolio review may stop a flagship initiative, but no final decision exists and rumours are affecting retention. What should you communicate?$qb$, $qb$State what is being reviewed, the decision criteria, what remains undecided, and when people can expect an update without implying false certainty.$qb$, $qb$Take a sensible immediate action on the visible issue and schedule the broader structural question for the next governance review.$qb$, $qb$Gather more evidence and make a limited adjustment, but leave the central trade-off or ownership unresolved.$qb$, $qb$Keep the current framework and ask affected leaders to manage the resulting consequences.$qb$, $qb$Maintain the current course until the risk becomes certain enough to force action.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
