  ($qb$ITEM-MCQ-25PLUS-R06-006$qb$, $qb$A3-03$qb$, $qb$MCQ$qb$, $qb$Two highly influential executives disagree so deeply on strategy that other leaders avoid taking positions for fear of joining a camp. What should the CEO do?$qb$, $qb$Reset the debate around shared evidence and enterprise criteria, address factional behavior explicitly, invite independent views, and make a clear decision without rewarding political alignment.$qb$, $qb$Apply the closest existing precedent with added safeguards, although it does not fully address the strategic context.$qb$, $qb$Escalate for a higher-level ruling before fully examining competing assumptions and consequences.$qb$, $qb$Choose the fastest workable compromise without addressing the underlying driver.$qb$, $qb$Protect the current target or position even if material risk is transferred elsewhere.$qb$, 5, 3, 2, 1, 0, true),
